.claude/worktrees/

# Build output. The Go broker is cross-compiled to a Windows binary for deployment to the dev VM
# (GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64), which drops a ~9MB mcp-server-win.exe straight into the source tree
# where a `git add -A` would happily commit it. Real release artifacts come from the (still unbuilt)
# release pipeline described in PRD §12, never from a developer's working tree.
mcp-server-win.exe
mcp-server-mac
*.exe

# Remote-mode dev runtime state (PRD §05) -- broker.json carries a live auth token, and this
# whole directory is per-machine runtime state anyway, same category as the platform app-data
# directory local mode writes to (never committed either).
Connectors/

# .NET build output, per TFM now that the Bridge multi-targets (PRD §11).
bin/
obj/
